I'm not sure whether you can use GOI in general with da clauses, nor really
{rV}, as {rV} operates at referent-level, not syntax-level.

Basically (as we noticed in the other thread), a *completely *logical usage
of {da} is not really very useful. The question is what exactly to relax to
make it more practical.

mu'o mi'e la latro'a

